# Iterate the product, not only the clerk

The stream review is a build loop. Read the think stream and last turn. If anything in the repo is blocking the desired result — tools, facts, gates, desktop, tests, wake bus, scorecard, persist, observability, IBKR/MDA split — **change it and test** (paper only). Do not wait for a “clerk bug” label. Same class as batch `option_quote`, full-book `option_facts`, lever snapshots, BAG, fill-lag ≠ flat, named `open_lots` on wake/last-turn.

Restart Pro only when the operator wants it on or RTH is useful. If Grok is looping tools or TWS is down, **kill** first — do not relaunch into a token burn.

Grok still owns the book: `send` quantity, `self_tune`. Do not grow the system prompt or inject strategy lectures. Do not flatten, enable live, or commit unless asked. There is no clerk process.
